title: 'transaction-storage-proof: read only the selected transaction'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    The storage-proof inherent used to read the target block's whole indexed body to prove one
    256-byte chunk. With renewals, that body can be about 1 GiB. The prover now uses the
    transaction sizes from `TransactionStorageApi::indexed_transactions` (v2) to pick the chunk
    and loads only the transaction that holds it. The proof is unchanged. Runtimes with API v1
    keep the old path. `IndexedBody` gains a required `indexed_transaction` method.
crates:
- name: sp-transaction-storage-proof
  bump: major
- name: sc-service
  bump: minor
- name: polkadot-omni-node-lib
  bump: minor
